DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with struct-based two-flag config.
  Both --exec-enabled and --diag-enabled must be supplied for the /exec
  endpoint to execute commands. The cmd query parameter is copied into a
  stack buffer via snprintf() and then passed to system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — two flags + struct):
  mechanism:  Two CLI flags (--exec-enabled, --diag-enabled) stored in
              struct diag_config fields (exec_enabled, diag_enabled)
  check:      double boolean guard in callback_exec():
              `if (!cfg->exec_enabled || !cfg->diag_enabled)`
  complexity: two conditions, one struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads cmd from request->map_url
              snprintf(cmd_buf, sizeof(cmd_buf), "%s", cmd) copies into buffer
              cmd_buf is then passed to system()
  transforms: one snprintf copy into a 1024-byte stack buffer; no sanitization
              of the content occurs during this copy

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system(cmd_buf) in callback_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — additions after callback_default():
    1. diag_config struct:  two exec gate fields (C2)
    2. callback_exec():     C2 two-flag gate + snprintf copy + system() (I2+S1)
    3. main():              two flag parsing into cfg struct + endpoint reg.

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18104 --exec-enabled --diag-enabled
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18104/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_104_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_104_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: supplying only one flag (or neither) causes /exec to return 403.
               Both --exec-enabled and --diag-enabled are required.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - The snprintf copy (I2) adds one indirection vs I1 but does not prevent
    injection: shell metacharacters pass through snprintf unchanged.
  - Payloads up to 1023 bytes fit in cmd_buf; longer payloads are silently
    truncated.
